# NEB-consistent ONE-SITE coadsorption model — REVIEW TEMPLATE ONLY
# New state names: R* = (H2O2)(C6H12)*; P* = (C6H12O)(H2O)*
# C6H14O2 is conserved for R* -> P*. Both require consistent absolute Gf.
# DO NOT RUN as-is: energy input and activities are unassigned.
#
# Proposed reaction expressions:
# rxn_expressions = [
#     '* + H2O2_g + C6H12_g <-> R*',
#     'R* -> P*',  # only when full NEB supports a barrierless route
#     'P* <-> C6H12O_g + H2O_g + *',
# ]
#
# For barriered cases substitute:
#     'R* <-> R-P* -> P*'  # R-P* is the VERIFIED saddle state
#
# Critical: CatMAP may clamp the effective TS free energy to max(IS,FS,TS).
# Any intermediate image lower than IS is NOT a negative activation barrier.
#
# Required before activating this model:
#  - Valid CatMAP energy file: absolute consistent Gf(R), Gf(P), gas products/reactants
#  - Adsorbate/capacity definitions, correctly conserved sites, gas activities
#  - NEB maximum over ALL images for each catalyst, or a justified barrierless rate rule
#  - Rigorous validation against experimental conditions
